From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:11:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: match Chrome broken-image dimensions

Track current-generation image failures and expose a synthetic 16 CSS-pixel
broken-image fallback without assigning natural dimensions or rendering an
icon. Empty alt suppresses the unsized fallback. Reset failure state on
source changes, including synchronous request-start failures.

Share image sizing between native width/height getters and element geometry.
Retain the existing unsigned-long reflection setters and their CE reactions;
honor CSS/HTML explicit dimensions, natural aspect ratios, detached/hidden
getter fallbacks, and whole-pixel image/offset dimensions. Detached images
have no layout box. Update the existing detached successful-image assertion
to expect its natural width; add no upstream tests.

Dispatch by the HTMLImageElement subtype, not the tag enum shared with SVG.
Invalidate cached document extents and schedule resize/intersection work in
the owning frame on image completion, source resets and alt mutations, with
teardown and request-generation guards intact.

This is synthetic layout, not image decoding, icon rasterization, complete
alt-text layout, or a general CSS replaced-element layout engine. The
benchmark is unchanged. Reference behavior was captured with local desktop
Chrome on Linux, not a macOS machine; the 16px fallback is in CSS pixels and
does not introduce any host-derived hardware persona values.

References:
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element
https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#extensions-to-the-htmlimageelement-interface

Validation: ReleaseFast build and all 1658 upstream tests pass. All 42
temporary cases pass, including 33 exact Chrome reference matches and nine
API-safety/observer/extent checks. The benchmark improves from 112/130 to
113/130 (86.92%), with only broken-image-dimensions changing verdict.
One reviewer pass found unsafe SVG dispatch and missing layout invalidation;
both were fixed and validated before export.
---
